{{--
    THE COREMEMORY WORDMARK — defined once per page.

    Why a shared <path> in <defs> rather than an <img> or two inline copies:

    1. `fill="currentColor"` means the one asset serves BOTH contexts — ink in
       the header, on-inverse in the footer — so the logo obeys tokens.css like
       everything else. An <img> cannot inherit colour, which would have meant
       two files and two hardcoded hex values, breaking the no-hex rule.
    2. The path is ~33 KB. Inlining it in the header AND the footer would pay
       that twice on every page; one <path> plus two <use> references pays it
       once, with no extra HTTP request.

    NOT a <symbol>. A <symbol> establishes its own viewport, so <use> drops it
    at x=0,y=0 sized 100%x100% of the CURRENT viewport — the rect y=0..959 in
    a coordinate system whose viewBox only shows y=-706..253. That left 26% of
    the wordmark visible and the rest outside the canvas. Referencing a plain
    <path> clones the geometry into the current user space with no nested
    viewport and no clipping, so these coordinates land exactly where the
    viewBox expects them.

    Rendered by <x-logo>, never used directly.
--}}
